# The runner's MIDI steps on stock behaviour: a knob turn sends its parameter out as NRPN (PARAM OUTPUT
# NRPN, ENCODER DEST INT+EXT), and an NRPN in sets the parameter without sending it back. rytm-emu's own
# settings are PARAM OUTPUT CC and ENCODER DEST INT, so the case sets them first with `emu` steps; a unit's
# MIDI settings are its owner's, so the case runs on the emulator only. Changes the BD sound's FRQ (64 at the
# end) and the emulator's MIDI settings (a snapshot each case: nothing kept).
name: link-midi-out
state: changes
target: emu

emu key GLOBAL
emu wait 500
emu key UP x12                      # GLOBAL opens on the row it was left on (REMOTE CTRL after the boot)
emu key DOWN x3                     # MIDI CONFIG
emu key YES
emu wait 500
emu key UP x4
emu key DOWN                        # PORT CONFIG
emu key YES
emu wait 500
emu key UP x12
emu key DOWN x6                     # PARAM OUTPUT: CC to NRPN
emu key LEFT
emu key DOWN                        # ENCODER DEST: INT to INT+EXT
emu key RIGHT
emu key NO x3
emu wait 500
hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key FLTR
cc 74 64
wait 3500
midi turn begin
nudge E +4 per 3                    # FRQ, by the knob
wait 750
midi turn end
expect turn has nrpn 1:20           # the turn goes out as FRQ's NRPN (1:20), on the auto channel
expect turn lacks cc 74
midi quiet begin
nrpn 1:20 64
wait 750
midi quiet end
expect quiet.count == 0             # a parameter set from MIDI is not sent back
